# The Zenodo concept DOI: it covers every version and resolves to the latest. Each release also gets its
# own version DOI on its Zenodo record; it is not pinned here, so this file never names a stale one.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23568348"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23568348"
    description: "Concept DOI: all versions of SetuHQ, archived on Zenodo"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ashfordeOU/SetuHQ"
url: "https://setuhq.com"
abstract: >-
  Open, reproducible transit search of public NASA TESS light curves. A calibrated
  reviewer panel of AI Sentinels (Claude by default; other providers supported and
  labelled) and deterministic matched-filter Probes marks every dip in blind-coded
  light curves, in the style of Planet Hunters; the pipeline then vets each dip, fits
  a limb-darkened transit model and bounds its false-alarm probability. It includes a
  frozen, blind benchmark of 662 real TESS Objects of Interest with controls, a public
  leaderboard with a catalogue-metadata floor, an all-sky sweep that classifies
  everything that dims, an MCP server and an app that maps every known exoplanet.
  Every output is a candidate, never a confirmation.
keywords:
  - exoplanets
  - transit search
  - TESS
  - benchmark
  - citizen science
  - large language models
